        "explanation": "JavaScript is not a traditional class-based OOP language like Java or C#. Instead, it is a Prototype-based OOP language. Objects inherit properties and methods directly from other objects via the 'Prototype Chain'. ES6 introduced the `class` keyword, but under the hood, it is just syntactic sugar over the existing prototypal inheritance system.",
