        "id": 73,
        "title": "What is the prototype chain?",
        "category": "Scope, Closures, Objects & DOM",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "The prototype chain is a series of links between objects. When you access a property on an object, the JS engine first checks the object itself. If not found, it traverses up the `__proto__` link to its prototype object. If not found there, it traverses to that prototype's prototype, and so on, until it reaches `Object.prototype`. The `__proto__` of `Object.prototype` is `null`, which ends the chain.",
