        "title": "What is deep copy?",
        "category": "Scope, Closures, Objects & DOM",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "A Deep Copy creates an entirely independent clone of an object or array, including all nested objects/arrays inside of it. The new object and the original object share absolutely no memory references. Modifying deeply nested data in the clone will not affect the original.",
