        "explanation": "Event Bubbling is a phase in the JS event propagation model. When an event happens on an element (like clicking a `<button>`), that event is handled by the button first, then it 'bubbles' up to its parent, then its grandparent, all the way up to the `document` object. Any event listeners attached to the parent elements will also fire sequentially from inside out.",
