        "explanation": "JavaScript is a single-threaded, synchronous language (it executes one line at a time on a single main thread). Asynchronous programming is a technique that allows JavaScript to initiate a long-running task (like fetching data from a database, reading a file, or waiting for a timer) and continue executing the rest of the code without waiting for that task to finish. When the task eventually finishes, a callback/promise alerts the main thread.",
