        "explanation": "A Promise (introduced in ES6) is a special JavaScript object representing the eventual completion (or failure) of an asynchronous operation and its resulting value. Instead of passing a callback into a function, a function returns a Promise object immediately. You then attach callbacks to that object using `.then()` for success and `.catch()` for failure.",
